# tree.zd — a branching tree that turns, with no JavaScript beside it.
#
# Move the controls and it re-grows: how many levels, how many branches
# leave each fork, and how fast the whole thing revolves. Nothing below is
# a callback and nothing below is a frame loop. The tree is a function of
# three signals, and the turning is a `@keyframes` in `assets/tree.css`.
#
# HOW A TREE IS DRAWN WITHOUT TRIGONOMETRY. This language has `sqrt` and
# `power` and no `sin` or `cos` at all, and the reason that does not matter
# is that **no branch here is ever placed absolutely.** Each branch is a
# child *element* of the branch it grows from, sitting at its parent's tip
# and rotated relative to it, so the browser multiplies each branch's
# rotation matrix by its parent's on the way down. A branch's direction in
# the world is composed by the compositor; the only thing this program has
# to name is a branch's angle *within its parent*, and with a fan of one to
# four there are exactly ten of those.
#
# So the split is not language and renderer any more. It is:
#
#   * **which branches exist** — the program's: a trunk and five nested
#     `each`es under it, one per level, recomputed from a signal;
#   * **where a branch points** — a class name per (fan, turn) pair, and
#     `assets/tree.css` turning ten of those into ten rotations.
#
# This is what used to be four parallel `List of Whole` handed to three.js
# through a `foreign … gives view`, on the argument that the trigonometry
# had to happen somewhere. It did not: nothing here needs a branch's
# absolute position, so nothing here needs the trigonometry that would
# produce one.
#
# THE TWO DOORS, AND WHY BOTH ARE ENOUGH. §6.1's `class is` takes a
# computed `Text`, not just a literal — `"zt-y" + (text of fan)` is a
# perfectly good class attribute — and everything under `assets/` ships
# with the bundle and is linked *after* the generated stylesheet, so a
# rule written there wins with no `!important`. Between them, anything CSS
# can express is expressible here, and rotation, perspective and animation
# are things CSS can express. There is no `transform` in the style
# vocabulary (§16.3) and there does not need to be.
#
# WHAT IS STILL NOT EXPRESSIBLE, HONESTLY. There is no per-frame signal —
# `clock` is read once at mount and #189 is open for a keyframe construct —
# so the revolve is a CSS animation rather than a derivation. That is the
# right home for it either way: the angle of the turntable is not state,
# nothing in the program branches on it, and a signal that ticked sixty
# times a second would recompute a tree that never changed.

# --- the three signals the page moves -------------------------------------
#
# Clamped where they are read *and* guarded where they are written. Read-side
# clamping alone is the bug this example used to have: the handler moved the
# raw signal past the limit, the derived one stopped, and the button looked
# dead for exactly as many presses as it had been overshot by. The guards
# below are what make that unreachable; the clamps stay as a net.

state depth  is client Whole starting 4
state spread is client Whole starting 3
state speed  is client Whole starting 3

# WHAT THIS COSTS, SAID PLAINLY. A branch is two DOM elements inside a
# `preserve-3d` subtree, which the compositor cannot flatten into one layer
# — so every branch is re-transformed every frame, and the budget is a few
# hundred of them rather than the few thousand a WebGL renderer would
# instance without noticing. Six levels of a four-way fan is 1365 branches
# and a slideshow. The ceiling therefore moves with the fan, so that the
# most the page can ask for is 364.
function ceilingFor of fan
    if fan >= 4
        give 5
    give 6

state fan     is client Whole from clamp with value is spread, low is 1, high is 4
state ceiling is client Whole from ceilingFor of fan
state levels  is client Whole from clamp with value is depth,  low is 1, high is ceiling
state pace    is client Whole from clamp with value is speed,  low is 1, high is 5

# --- which branches exist -------------------------------------------------

# `[0, 1, … bound - 1]`, built in tail position so the emitter turns the
# last call into a jump.
function countUp with bound, index, taken
    if index >= bound
        give taken
    give countUp with bound is bound, index is index + 1, taken is (append index to taken)

# The turns a branch at `level` fans into: `fan` of them while the tree is
# grown that far, and none at all once it is not. Emptying the list is what
# ends the recursion — a level with no turns has no children, so the five
# nested `each`es below need no depth test of their own.
function turnsAt with level, levels, fan
    if level > levels
        give empty
    give countUp with bound is fan, index is 0, taken is empty

state turns2 is client List of Whole from turnsAt with level is 2, levels is levels, fan is fan
state turns3 is client List of Whole from turnsAt with level is 3, levels is levels, fan is fan
state turns4 is client List of Whole from turnsAt with level is 4, levels is levels, fan is fan
state turns5 is client List of Whole from turnsAt with level is 5, levels is levels, fan is fan
state turns6 is client List of Whole from turnsAt with level is 6, levels is levels, fan is fan

# --- the class names ------------------------------------------------------

# A branch says two things about itself and neither is a number of degrees:
# how deep it is, which decides its length, its thickness and its colour,
# and which way round its parent it leaves, which decides its rotation.
# `zt-d3 zt-y4-2` is "level three, turn two of a four-way fan".
function limb with level, fan, turn
    give "zt-b zt-d" + (text of level) + " zt-y" + (text of fan) + "-" + (text of turn)

# A step that would do nothing says so, rather than looking broken.
function step of atLimit
    if atLimit
        give "zt-step zt-step-spent"
    give "zt-step"

# --- how many branches that is --------------------------------------------
#
# The one thing on the page that is genuinely computed rather than
# described: 1 + f + f² + … + f^(levels-1), accumulated a row at a time.
function branchCount with levels, fan, level, row, total
    if level >= levels
        give total
    give branchCount with levels is levels,
        fan is fan,
        level is level + 1,
        row is row * fan,
        total is total + (row * fan)

state count is client Whole from branchCount with levels is levels,
    fan is fan,
    level is 1,
    row is 1,
    total is 1

# --- the page -------------------------------------------------------------

view title is "A tree that turns"
    Column class is "zt-page", font is "system", padding is 28, gap is 22
        Column gap is 6
            Heading "A tree that turns"
            Text "Six levels of nesting, ten class names and one CSS keyframe. Every branch is an element, every angle is relative to its parent, and no JavaScript ships with this program.",
                color is "muted",
                size is "small",
                lineHeight is 1.55

        # The stage. Everything inside it is a branch; the perspective, the
        # colours and the revolve are `assets/tree.css`.
        #
        # The bare `zt-x` under each branch is that branch's second blade,
        # crossed through the first at ninety degrees. One blade is flat, and
        # a flat branch becomes a hairline every time the turntable brings it
        # edge-on — which is a quarter of every revolution, on every branch.
        # It is the one element here that is scenery rather than structure.
        Column class is "zt-stage",
            position is "relative",
            overflow is "clip",
            height is 440,
            radius is 18,
            border is 1,
            borderColor is "line",
            shadow is "high"
            Column class is ("zt-turn zt-sp" + (text of pace))
                Column class is ("zt-root zt-fit" + (text of levels))
                    Column class is "zt-b zt-d1"
                        Column class is "zt-x"
                        each a in turns2
                            Column class is (limb with level is 2, fan is fan, turn is a)
                                Column class is "zt-x"
                                each b in turns3
                                    Column class is (
                                        limb with level is 3,
                                        fan is fan,
                                        turn is b)
                                        Column class is "zt-x"
                                        each c in turns4
                                            Column class is (
                                                limb with level is 4,
                                                fan is fan,
                                                turn is c)
                                                Column class is "zt-x"
                                                each d in turns5
                                                    Column class is (
                                                        limb with level is 5,
                                                        fan is fan,
                                                        turn is d)
                                                        Column class is "zt-x"
                                                        each e in turns6
                                                            Column class is (
                                                                limb with level is 6,
                                                                fan is fan,
                                                                turn is e)
                                                                Column class is "zt-x"

        Row gap is 14, align is "stretch"
            Column grow is 1,
                basis is 0,
                gap is 10,
                padding is 14,
                radius is 14,
                background is "raised",
                border is 1,
                borderColor is "line"
                Text "levels", color is "muted", size is "small"
                Row gap is 8, align is "center"
                    Button "−",
                        class is (step of (depth <= 1)),
                        padding is 6,
                        width is 38,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if depth > 1
                                subtract 1 from depth
                    Button "+",
                        class is (step of (depth >= ceiling)),
                        padding is 6,
                        width is 38,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if depth < ceiling
                                add 1 to depth
                    Text levels, class is "zt-readout", size is "large", weight is "600"

            Column grow is 1,
                basis is 0,
                gap is 10,
                padding is 14,
                radius is 14,
                background is "raised",
                border is 1,
                borderColor is "line"
                Text "branches per fork", color is "muted", size is "small"
                Row gap is 8, align is "center"
                    Button "−",
                        class is (step of (spread <= 1)),
                        padding is 6,
                        width is 38,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if spread > 1
                                subtract 1 from spread
                    # Raising the fan to four lowers the ceiling to five, so
                    # the depth comes down with it here rather than being
                    # clamped on the way out — otherwise `depth` would sit at
                    # six while the tree showed five, and the next press of
                    # `−` would move the signal and change nothing on screen.
                    Button "+",
                        class is (step of (spread >= 4)),
                        padding is 6,
                        width is 38,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if spread < 4
                                add 1 to spread
                                if depth > 5
                                    set depth to 5
                    Text fan, class is "zt-readout", size is "large", weight is "600"

            Column grow is 1,
                basis is 0,
                gap is 10,
                padding is 14,
                radius is 14,
                background is "raised",
                border is 1,
                borderColor is "line"
                Text "revolutions", color is "muted", size is "small"
                Row gap is 8, align is "center"
                    Button "slower",
                        class is (step of (speed <= 1)),
                        padding is 6,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if speed > 1
                                subtract 1 from speed
                    Button "faster",
                        class is (step of (speed >= 5)),
                        padding is 6,
                        radius is 10,
                        background is "surface",
                        border is 1,
                        borderColor is "line",
                        color is "ink",
                        hoverBackground is "raised"
                        on click
                            if speed < 5
                                add 1 to speed
                    Text pace, class is "zt-readout", size is "large", weight is "600"

        Row gap is 6, align is "center"
            Text "branches:", color is "muted", size is "small"
            Text count, class is "zt-readout", size is "small", weight is "600"
